  "findings": [
    "Canonical F32-to-F16 cache conversion matches independent nearest-even conversion on both GPUs. Earlier input differences become larger after cache quantization; this is not evidence of a conversion defect.",
    "Identical Q4K prefill operands differ across platforms. A test-only four-lane FMA accumulation improves agreement and Float64-reference error. Its accumulators match exactly; its final reduction differs.",
    "An ordered final reduction makes the captured projection bit-identical. Whole-model qualification still fails, and forward results worsen. Isolated-operation success is not sufficient.",
    "The captured decode Q4K GEMV is bit-identical across platforms without arithmetic substitution.",
    "With ordered projection and refined normalization experiments, all 19 layer-zero input-normalization and QKV projection rows match. All captured linear-attention inputs and initial state match. Convolution sum matches; exp, denominator and reciprocal differ.",
    "Recurrent execution differs with identical captured inputs, independently of convolution differences.",
    "The test-only SiLU polynomial reduces differing convolution elements but increases the largest cross-platform difference. It remains unaccepted and covers only the captured finite operand range."
  ],
